    <p class="section-intro">Add these two methods to your Player class.</p>
    
    <!-- 1. choose_action -->
    <details class="skeleton-block" open>
        <summary class="skeleton-summary">
            <span class="skeleton-step">1</span>
            <span class="skeleton-title">choose_action (Selection Hook)</span>
            <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down skeleton-chevron"></i>
        </summary>
        <div class="skeleton-content">
            <div class="skeleton-line code">METHOD choose_action(options_list) → integer:</div>
            <div class="skeleton-desc">
                <strong>Purpose:</strong> Let the player pick a combat move.<br>
                <strong>Logic:</strong> This works exactly like <code>respond_to_npc</code>!
                <ul>
                    <li>Display the options with numbers</li>
                    <li>Ask the user for input</li>
                    <li>Validate it's a number and in range</li>
                    <li>Return the 0-based index</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </details>
    
    <!-- 2. compute_damage -->
    <details class="skeleton-block">
        <summary class="skeleton-summary">
            <span class="skeleton-step">2</span>
            <span class="skeleton-title">compute_damage (Calculation Hook)</span>
            <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down skeleton-chevron"></i>
        </summary>
        <div class="skeleton-content">
            <div class="skeleton-line code">METHOD compute_damage(base_damage, armour) → integer:</div>
            <div class="skeleton-desc">
                <strong>Requirement:</strong> Calculate damage: <code>Damage = Base - Armour</code><br>
                <strong>Constraint:</strong> Damage cannot be negative! Use <code>max()</code> function.
                <div class="skeleton-line code" style="margin-top: 0.5rem;">damage = base_damage - armour</div>
                <div class="skeleton-line code">return MAX(0, damage)</div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </details>
</section>

